👉 “Why Tailwind uses rem instead of px?”

answer:Because rem is responsive and scales with root font size, making UI more accessible and consistent across devices.
and p-3 means i   px  will be 3x4 18px we have to multiply by 4 four fig  out what pixel it is 

Class	    Value(rem)	        Pixels
p-1     	0.25rem	            4px
p-2	        0.5rem	            8px
p-4	        1rem	            16px
p-6	        1.5rem	            24px
p-8	        2rem	            32px

this is the types of the padding we are using in the tailwind css 
p-8 → all sides (top, right, bottom, left)
px-8 → left + right
py-8 → top + bottom
pt-8 → top only
pb-8 → bottom only


